Show which profile is playing: a line in the main menu footer, a short message when EmulationStation starts, and a permanent badge.

Nothing is added when profiles are not in use (no named profile exists and the default one is active), so single-user setups see
nothing new.  The name comes from GuiProfilesSettings::getActiveProfileLabel(), which reads the same files as the profile screen
(display_name, then the RetroAchievements username, then the folder name).

* Main menu footer: "Profile: <name>" next to the version text.
* Start-up message: a six-second alert when EmulationStation starts.
* Badge: a permanent alert-style label (just the name) in the FIRST slot of the notification stack, so the other alerts (now
  playing, update available) appear below it.  It uses the menu theme's own background, font and colours, so it follows whatever theme
  is installed.  Hidden while a menu or dialog is open.  Setting "ProfileBadge" (auto / on / off), in the user interface settings:
  auto shows it when there are profiles, on shows it always, off never.  It is kept out of the alert list so the power saver still
  resumes, and it is not read aloud.

One patch on purpose: the pieces change the same lines, and the applier detects "already applied" by reverse-checking each patch.
